<title>SWITZERLAND: Winterthur says 1996 net rose 21 pct.</title>
<headline>Winterthur says 1996 net rose 21 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			506.7	     vs 419.2</p>
<p> Gross premiums		 25,949.6	  vs 22,310.2</p>
<p> Div (regd, Sfr)		21		  vs 19</p>
<p> Earnings per share (Sfr)   57		  vs 48</p>
<p> Financial result	     5,521.4	   vs 4,676.0</p>
<p>Profit before tax, minorities,</p>
<p>  bond interest		 984.1	     vs 815.7</p>
<p>  - Non-life		    618.2	     vs 580.4</p>
<p>  - Life			  365.9	     vs 235.3</p>
<p> Investments		    85,623.3	  vs 71,937.3</p>
<p> Technical provisions	 80,411.2	  vs 67,535.4</p>
<p> Shareholder equity	   5,172.2	   vs 4,030.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Winterthur Insurance Co said gross premiums in non-life business grew 18 percent and exceeded 15 billion Swiss francs for the first time. It said life insurance gross premiums rose 14 percent to over 10 billion francs.</p>
<p>Winterthur said it would present more detailed numbers on 1996 results at an annual news conference on May 29. -- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
